---
// Help with drugs or alcohol, and free Narcan (#477, rank 2 in #475). Today
// (an overdose, free naloxone), then treatment and help lines. Facts are in
// resource records or quoted below with their sources, read 2026-10-30.
// High-stakes topic (names 911 and 988): the PR waits for David (#97).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ResourceCard from '../components/ResourceCard.astro';
import SourceLine from '../components/SourceLine.astro';
import { loadDir } from '../lib/content.mjs';
export const page = { door: "care", topic: "health", label: "Drugs or alcohol help", summary: "An overdose, free Narcan, detox and treatment, help lines" };
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const all = loadDir('resources');
const r = (slug) => all.find((e) => e.slug === slug);
const overdoseSources = [
  { url: 'https://helpandhopewv.org/what-can-you-do/naloxone/', checked: '2026-10-30' },
  { url: 'https://www.cdc.gov/stop-overdose/response/index.html', checked: '2026-10-30', name: 'CDC' },
  { url: 'https://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-approves-first-over-counter-naloxone-nasal-spray', checked: '2026-10-30', name: 'FDA' },
];
const lawSources = [
  { url: 'https://code.wvlegislature.gov/16-47-4/', checked: '2026-10-30', name: 'West Virginia Code §16-47-4' },
  { url: 'https://code.wvlegislature.gov/16-47-5/', checked: '2026-10-30', name: 'West Virginia Code §16-47-5' },
];
---
<Base crisis title="Help with drugs or alcohol in Morgantown and Mon County, and free Narcan" description="Drug and alcohol help in Morgantown and Monongalia County: what to do in an overdose, free naloxone (Narcan) from the Mon County health department, detox and treatment at Valley HealthCare and WVU Medicine, and free 24/7 help lines.">
  <h1>Help with drugs or alcohol</h1>
  <p class="lede">Someone overdosing? Call <a href="tel:911">911</a>. Naloxone (Narcan) is free from the Mon County Health Department. For treatment, call Valley HealthCare at <a href="tel:3042961731">304-296-1731</a> or WVU Medicine's Chestnut Ridge Center at <a href="tel:3045984214">304-598-4214</a>.</p>

  <h2>If someone may be overdosing</h2>
  <p>West Virginia's Help and Hope site says to call 911 right away if a person has any of these signs:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Their face is very pale or feels clammy</li>
    <li>Their lips or fingernails are purple or blue</li>
    <li>They cannot be woken up or cannot speak</li>
    <li>Their breathing or heartbeat slows or stops</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The CDC says to give naloxone if you have it and call 911, try to keep the person awake and breathing, lay them on their side so they do not choke, and stay with them until help arrives.</p>
  <p>Naloxone nasal spray is sold over the counter, with no prescription. The FDA approved this in 2023.</p>
  <SourceLine sources={overdoseSources} about="what to do in an overdose" />

  <h3>Calling 911 for an overdose</h3>
  <p>West Virginia law says a person who calls for emergency help, in good faith and in time, for someone who seems to be overdosing cannot be held criminally responsible for some crimes. These include having drugs without a prescription and some underage drinking crimes. To be covered, the caller must stay with the person until help comes, give their name if asked, and cooperate. It does not cover every crime. The person who overdosed can get the same protection if they take part in and finish a treatment or recovery program the court approves. Read the law for the details.</p>
  <SourceLine sources={lawSources} about="the overdose 911 law" />

  <h2>Get free naloxone (Narcan)</h2>
  {r('monchd-free-naloxone') && <ResourceCard r={r('monchd-free-naloxone')} />}

  <h2>Help lines, any hour</h2>
  {r('help4wv') && <ResourceCard r={r('help4wv')} sms={r('help4wv').contact.text} smsLabel="Text HELP4WV" />}
  {r('samhsa-national-helpline') && <ResourceCard r={r('samhsa-national-helpline')} />}

  <h2>Detox and treatment in Mon County</h2>
  {r('valley-substance-use-treatment') && <ResourceCard r={r('valley-substance-use-treatment')} />}
  {r('wvu-addiction-treatment') && <ResourceCard r={r('wvu-addiction-treatment')} />}
  <p>On Medicaid or have other insurance? Ask each place whether they take your plan before your first visit. No insurance? The SAMHSA helpline above can refer you to state-funded treatment or places with a sliding fee.</p>

  <h2>Also check</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Thinking about suicide, or in a mental health crisis? Call or text <a href="tel:988">988</a>, any hour.</li>
    <li>Low income and no insurance: <a href={`${base}/dental-and-prescriptions/`}>the free Health Right clinic</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="meta">Sources checked October 30, 2026. We describe these services and the law; we do not give medical or legal advice. Call first, since hours and programs change. Something out of date? <a href="https://github.com/david-shortman/mon-county-community-hub/issues/new?template=suggest-resource.yml">Tell us</a>.</p>
</Base>
